<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia Apr private sector credit rises 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Australia Apr private sector credit rises 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) said private sector credit extended by financial intermediaries rose by 1.0 percent in April, seasonally-adjusted, after rising 0.7 percent in March.</p>
<p>For the year to April credit rose by 9.5 percent.  </p>
<p>The RBA detailed the change in financial aggregates as follows, seasonally-adjusted in percentage terms --</p>
<p>				     Apr 97	Mar 97   Apr 97/Apr 96</p>
<p>    Total credit		 +1.0	  +0.7	   +9.5</p>
<p>    M3			     +1.6	  -0.3	   +9.8</p>
<p>    Broad money		  +1.6	  -0.1	  +10.2</p>
<p>-- Private Sector Credit</p>
<p>    Housing			+1.1	  +0.7	  +10.6</p>
<p>    Business		     +1.0	  +0.6	   +8.3</p>
<p>    Other Personal use	 +0.3	  +0.7	  +11.4</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
